# SkillLedger Cursor Rules

## Port Configuration - CRITICAL

**ALWAYS use these ports for SkillLedger to avoid conflicts with other projects:**

- Backend API HTTP: `8030`
- Backend API HTTPS: `8031`
- Frontend Client: `3030`
- SQL Server (Docker): `9030`
- SQL Server (Windows): `localhost\SQLEXPRESS01` (named instance)

## Multi-Project Port Allocation Strategy

When working across multiple projects, maintain this port allocation:

1. **SkillLedger**: Backend 8030, Client 3030, SQL 9030

### Port Pattern Rules
- Backend API: `80X0` (X = project number 1-6)
- Frontend Client: `30X0` (X = project number 1-6)
- Mobile App: `50Y0` (Y varies)
- SQL Server: `90X0` (X = project number 1-6)

## Configuration Files to Check

When changing ports, update these files:
- `src/SkillLedger.Api/Properties/launchSettings.json` - Backend ports
- `src/SkillLedger.Api/appsettings.json` - BaseUrl and CORS
- `src/SkillLedger.Api/appsettings.Development.json` - BaseUrl, CORS, JWT audience
- `web/package.json` - Frontend dev script port (-p 3030)
- `web/next.config.js` - API proxy destination
- `docker-compose.yml` - SQL Server port mapping
- `start-windows-dev.ps1` - Documentation in startup script

## Development Standards

### Test-Driven Development (TDD)
- Write tests FIRST for all critical paths
- Follow Red-Green-Refactor cycle
- Security, business logic, and financial calculations MUST have tests before implementation

### Definition of Done
- ✅ All tests passing (100%)
- ✅ Zero linter errors
- ✅ Build successful (frontend & backend)
- ✅ Code committed with descriptive message

### Git Workflow
- Commit ALL related changes together (check `git status`)
- Write descriptive commit messages
- Include footer: `🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)`

## Architecture
- Clean Architecture with domain-driven design
- Enterprise security (CSRF, rate limiting, audit logging)
- Azure services integration (Key Vault, App Insights, Communication Services)
- Financial compliance and tax reporting capabilities

## Documentation
See `CLAUDE.md` for complete project configuration and standards.


